        "original_id": "457de491-6ec4-5db6-8eb5-b08e40951862",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arlette Roxburgh, Francis Scott Key\n- Organizations: New Jersey Devils, Royal Navy\n- Places: Fort McHenry, Baltimore Harbor, United States of America\n- Concepts: The Star-Spangled Banner, Defence of Fort M'Henry, Battle of Baltimore, War of 1812, national anthem\n\nFacts:\n- On September 14, 1814, Francis Scott Key wrote the poem \"Defence of Fort M'Henry\" after witnessing the bombardment of Fort McHenry by British Royal Navy ships in Baltimore Harbor during the Battle of Baltimore in the War of 1812.\n- \"The Star-Spangled Banner\" is the national anthem of the United States of America.\n- The lyrics of \"The Star-Spangled Banner\" come from Francis Scott Key's poem \"Defence of Fort M'Henry.\"\n- Arlette Roxburgh is best known for singing \"The Star-Spangled Banner\" before every New Jersey Devils home game started.",
